ENGLISH
========================================================================

0. DEFINITIONS

"Engine": the Cramion source code and binaries published by the
Licensor (CramionCore, CramionFX, CramionDM, CramionEditor,
CramionUpdater, the player, tools, templates, shaders, documentation
and accompanying resources), including modified versions of them.

"Licensor": Josin (MantraxStudios), author and copyright holder of the
Engine.

"Product": a game, application, interactive experience, visualization
or content created WITH the Engine whose primary value is its own
content and not the Engine itself.

"Runtime": the parts of the Engine a Product needs in order to run (the
exported player, its libraries, and the shaders and data the editor
generates on export).

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO (free of charge, royalty-free)

a) Use the Engine and the editor for any purpose, personal or
   commercial.
b) Create Products and sell, publish or distribute them, for free or
   for a fee, on any store or platform, without paying royalties to the
   Licensor.
c) Include the Runtime in your Products in compiled form.
d) Read, study and modify the Engine source code for your own Products.
e) Share the Engine source code, original or modified, ONLY free of
   charge and publicly (for example, a fork on GitHub), together with
   this full license and without removing copyright notices.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

a) Sell, rent, sublicense or charge in any way (including mandatory
   donations, subscriptions, "packs", paywalls or early access) for the
   Engine, the editor or their source code, original or modified,
   whether alone or inside a package, course, template or bundle whose
   main content is the Engine.
b) Distribute the editor or the Engine tools as part of a Product,
   except for the Runtime.
c) Present the Engine, or a modified version of it, as your own work,
   or rename it to offer it as a different engine or tool.
d) Remove, hide or alter this license notice, the copyright notices or
   the Engine credits.
e) Use the name "Cramion", its logos or its visual identity for any
   product other than the official Engine, except as allowed in
   TRADEMARK.md.
f) Publish the Engine, or substantial parts of its code, on asset
   stores, marketplaces or other sales platforms.

3. ATTRIBUTION

Products do not have to show a Cramion logo or splash screen. It is
enough to include in their credits, or in a license file next to the
executable, the phrase "Made with Cramion Engine" and the third-party
notices the Runtime requires (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

4. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Engine uses third-party libraries that keep their own licenses (see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). This license does not restrict the rights
those licenses grant you over those components.

5. EARLIER VERSIONS

Engine versions up to and including 1.4 were released under the MIT
license and remain governed by it. This license applies to version 1.5
and every later version, and to any code added or changed from then on.

6. TERMINATION

If you breach this license, your rights end automatically. Products you
already released in compliance with it keep their permission to be
distributed. The Licensor may report any unauthorized copy or sale to
the relevant platforms and authorities.

7. NO WARRANTY

THE ENGINE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL
THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING
FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE ENGINE OR ITS USE.

8. ADDITIONAL PERMISSIONS

For any use not covered here (for example, a license to redistribute
the Engine commercially), contact the Licensor:
https://github.com/MantraxStudios/Cramion or the official Discord
(https://discord.gg/zG7rSsUGEz).
